            <ArticleTitle>Guide catheter damage during rotational coronary atherectomy of aorto-ostial lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>649-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two cases in which the tips of guide catheters were damaged by rotational burrs during rotational coronary atherectomy of aorto-ostial lesions. There were no signs of embolization caused by the material of the guide catheters during and after the interventions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
